row(11, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'AND WHAT HE DID TO THE ARMY OF EGYPT, ITS HORSES AND ITS CHARIOT — HOW HE MADE THE WATERS OF THE RED SEA FLOW OVER THEM WHEN THEY PURSUED AFTER YOU, AND THE LORD DESTROYED THEM TO THIS DAY. {HP(11, 4, (("לחיל", "מצרים", "לסוסיו", "ולרכבו"), "the army of Egypt, its horses and its chariot — the pair with the suffixes one seat (Exodus 14:23 \'every horse of Pharaoh, his chariot\')"), (("אשר", "הציף", "את", "מי", "ים", "סוף"), "how He MADE the waters of the Red Sea FLOW over — the hiphil\'s one seat in the Bible (the root\'s other two: the axe-head floated, 2 Kings 6:6; the waters flowed over Lamentations\' head, 3:54); \'the waters of the Red Sea\' 11:4 and JOSHUA 2:10 — RAHAB\'S seat; the Red Sea three in the book"), (("ברדפם", "אחריכם"), "when they pursued after you — one seat"), (("ויאבדם", "יהוה", "עד", "היום", "הזה"), "and the LORD destroyed them to this day — the wayyiqtol, the chapter\'s first of two; \'to this day\' six in the book"))} {AP(11, 4, (("למשרית", "מצרים"), "the CAMP of Egypt — for the army (ten seats of the word in the book)"), (("די", "אטיף", "ית", "מי", "ימא", "דסוף"), "how He made the waters of the Sea of Reeds flow"), (("ואובדנון", "יי"), "and the LORD destroyed them"))} THE SEA TOLD IN NEW WORDS: no verse of Exodus 14-15 shares more than three tokens with the retelling (14:31\'s three; 14:28 and 15:19 two) — the readback\'s row against the sea\'s line (Exodus 14:21-31) owed to the compile, the closest kin in the Bible 34:6\'s \'to this day\' (four) and Joshua 24:6 (three).')
